  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Crandall University is in Canada, New Brunswick. It is a non-profit Christian Liberal Arts institution. Currently, the establishment offers higher education courses at Bachelorâ€™s and Masterâ€™s levels. The university also provides programs for subjects such as Education, Business and Science.<br><br>The institution also has a small intake of students, around 1,000. As a result, an intimate, close and welcoming community exists on campus with small classes taking place. There are also plenty of extracurricular activities and options available on and off campus.</p><h2>What is the Crandall University acceptance rate?</h2><p>The Crandall University acceptance rate is 70-80%.</p> <p>In its 200-acre campus, Crandall provides students with top-level higher-education facilities. Also, the Baptist Heritage Center has various specialist materials, such as paintings, furniture, service materials and musical instruments.<br><br>Students will also find laboratories with scientific equipment to aid studies. Furthermore, the campus has various sports facilities. Gyms are available for use at each hall of residence.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p><p>Crandall University has an active and welcoming campus. Students are also encouraged to become part of the universityâ€™s community through various clubs, organisations or sports teams.<br><br>Many faith-based clubs are available for students as the university stays true to its Christian roots. As a result, students can participate in various services and discussion clubs. Also, students can take part in voluntary activities that give back to the campus and the local community. Alternatively, Crandall has many other clubs, including soccer, basketball, boxing, cross country and more.</p>"
